WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.333
- All right,

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:03.430
- we can't end the hour without
one last feel good story.

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.159
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.159 --> 00:00:08.376
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:11.350
Many of the greatest guitarists
in rock and roll history

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.790
have humble roots.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.780
Eddie Van Halen hand-made
his first guitar.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.613
As a kid,

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:17.730
Keith Richard stacked books

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.780
to reach his grandfather's
guitar on a high shelf.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.560
And Jimi Hendrix's first guitar

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.360
only had one string,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.330
but throughout history,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.970
we've never witnessed the
birth of a rock and roll legend

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:28.870
in real time.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.270
That is until this year.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.023
People, witness history.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.001
- Oh, he's playing a little rock music.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.770
(kid exclaiming) (guitar strings plucking)

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.883
- Wow.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.574
Wow.

00:00:44.574 --> 00:00:47.574
(audience laughing)

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.420
All right, coming to the end.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.357
All right, everybody give him a hand!

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:10.447
- Little man was rocking
so hard. He was shaking.

00:01:10.447 --> 00:01:13.040
I've got to get Jocko's reaction, Jocko.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.270
Do you think he has what it takes?

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.810
- That guy is awesome. (laughing)

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.990
- That's full heat!

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.070
And I love that he just kept
going, like, you're like,

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:20.903
okay, I get it.

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:22.176
Nope.

00:01:22.176 --> 00:01:23.009
I'm gonna keep going!

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:24.910
- The teacher kept going, oh, oh.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:25.743
Oh.

00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:29.670
He turned the guitar up
and started (laughing)

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.740
- He's got all the moves!

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.690
- Oh my God, he's so great.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.330
The little boy's name is Crew.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.980
Better known as Rock On Crew.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.920
And we have him on the line
along with his mama Hannah.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.790
So Hannah.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.210
Oh my gosh. You are so gorgeous.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.210
So the teacher's reaction was hilarious.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.750
Was she slightly scared?

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.810
- That is a great question.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.350
So I prepared her a little bit

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.252
because Crew has always loved rock music.

00:01:56.252 --> 00:01:58.250
And I told her right before,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.160
because I wasn't allowed to be there.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.190
I said, you know,

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.940
he's got a special song
prepared for you guys.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.360
And she told me right
after, she's like, you know,

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.900
I wasn't really prepared for that,

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.100
but I thought he maybe
like got his fingers caught

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.120
in the strings and leaned over to check.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.940
Yeah. Just like that.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.773
And she says,

00:02:16.773 --> 00:02:19.847
but then after I realized he
was just feeling the music.

00:02:19.847 --> 00:02:21.186
(audience laughing)

00:02:21.186 --> 00:02:22.060
- Oh my gosh. It's amazing.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.830
So there was a song you
were supposed to sing.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.133
So how did it go?

00:02:28.516 --> 00:02:32.016
(unintelligible kid talk)

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:36.822
- Thank you teachers,
we love you teachers.

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:40.560
- You are so amazing, little man!

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.610
Oh my God.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.050
So where do you think Crew
gets his inspiration here?

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.050
Are y'all just like rocking out at home?

00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:49.564
- Yeah. Yeah, tell her.

00:02:49.564 --> 00:02:50.731
- The rockers!

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.680
- He tells me that rockers
give him inspiration,

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.560
but really who taught him, is?

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.393
- Daddy!

00:02:57.393 --> 00:02:58.816
- Daddy taught him.

00:02:58.816 --> 00:02:59.649
(audience clapping)

00:02:59.649 --> 00:03:00.487
- Awww!

00:03:00.487 --> 00:03:01.570
- Yeah. I grew up-

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.777
- Let me do it!

00:03:02.777 --> 00:03:05.888
My mom grow up playing the piano.

00:03:05.888 --> 00:03:09.101
My dad grow up playing drums.

00:03:09.101 --> 00:03:11.851
And he loved rocker music better.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.736
- Yeah, I grew up playing the piano.

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:17.336
My husband grew up playing the drums

00:03:17.336 --> 00:03:21.620
and so Crew naturally
loves rock music better.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.597
- Oh my gosh. Well Crew,

00:03:23.597 --> 00:03:26.440
at some point you're going
to have to come on our show

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.980
and you're going to have
to play with my band.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.810
This would be amazing is all I'm saying.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.120
If you came and rocked out with
us, would you be into that?

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.651
- Say yeah!

00:03:34.651 --> 00:03:35.484
- Yeah!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.820
- All right, thank you so much, Hannah.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.540
And thanks Rock On Crew

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.880
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.460
He's getting his fingers ready. I love it.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.420
That's not all though!

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.560
Our season long partner,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.360
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.280
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.230
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers, just like Crew.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.330
So they're going to be writing you

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.424
a check for a thousand dollars.

00:03:57.424 --> 00:04:00.280
(audience cheering)

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.900
Crew, this is your first paying gig.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.733
Yeah!

